cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Fall-Relay, please cite it as below."
title: "Fall-Relay: Edge–server software for reliable fall-event delivery and alert management"
type: software
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/inha0307/fall-relay"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23719976
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23719976"
abstract: "Fall-Relay delivers fall alerts from a camera-equipped Raspberry Pi to the web browsers of responders and records how each alert is handled. The device stores each fall event in a local transactional outbox and resends it until the server confirms storage; the server recognises a resent message by its identifier, so a duplicate never raises a second alert. The alert has its own lifecycle, separate from the fall event, and remains unresolved until a responder acknowledges it and records an outcome. A simulated example and automated fault-injection tests run without a camera or a trained model."
keywords:
  - fall detection
  - edge computing
  - reliable event delivery
  - transactional outbox
  - alert management
  - Raspberry Pi
